  "period_note": "Year-end position from the Annual Report's own multi-year 'Key operating and financial data' summary table (audited), cross-validated against the Balance Sheet wherever available. This bank has operated with deeply negative shareholders' equity and a deeply negative Capital Adequacy Ratio (CAR) throughout the entire researched period (2013-2024), i.e. it has been technically insolvent by conventional accounting/regulatory measures for over a decade — a legacy of the 2006 collapse and nationalization of its predecessor, The Oriental Bank Limited, on fraud/mismanagement grounds. As a Shariah-based Islamic bank, reports 'Investment' rather than conventional 'Loans and Advances', and 'Classified Investments' rather than 'NPL'. Total shareholders' equity here uses Tier-I core capital as reported, cross-verified as equal to paid-up capital + statutory reserve + general reserve + retained earnings (i.e. no material regulatory deductions applied for this institution), so treated as equivalent to accounting shareholders' equity for this and the following year. Total liabilities not directly reported for this year; calculated as total assets minus this equity figure.",
